{"tool_name":"dca","contents":["biocontainers","oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"dca","identifiers":["doi:10.1101/300681"],"license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"Count autoencoder for scRNA-seq denoising","home_url":"https://github.com/theislab/dca","keywords":["RNA-Seq"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"DCA","home":"https://github.com/theislab/dca","license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"Deep count autoencoder for denoising scRNA-seq data.","addition_date":"2019-06-30T13:21:36Z","last_update_date":"2019-06-30T13:21:36Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:DCA","cost":"Free of charge","documentation":[{"note":"Tutorial material","type":["Training material"],"url":"https://github.com/theislab/dca/blob/master/tutorial.ipynb"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"cmd":"dca matrix.csv results","input":[{"data":{"term":"Gene expression matrix","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3112"},"format":[{"term":"TSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3475"}]}],"note":"Run DCA on CSV/TSV-formatted raw count matrix with genes in rows and cells in columns.","operation":[{"term":"Imputation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3557"},{"term":"Statistical modelling","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3664"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Gene expression matrix","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3112"},"format":[{"term":"TSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3475"}]}]}],"maturity":"Emerging","name":"DCA","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-018-07931-2","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2019, The Author(s).Single-cell RNA sequencing (scRNA-seq) has enabled researchers to study gene expression at a cellular resolution. However, noise due to amplification and dropout may obstruct analyses, so scalable denoising methods for increasingly large but sparse scRNA-seq data are needed. We propose a deep count autoencoder network (DCA) to denoise scRNA-seq datasets. DCA takes the count distribution, overdispersion and sparsity of the data into account using a negative binomial noise model with or without zero-inflation, and nonlinear gene-gene dependencies are captured. Our method scales linearly with the number of cells and can, therefore, be applied to datasets of millions of cells. We demonstrate that DCA denoising improves a diverse set of typical scRNA-seq data analyses using simulated and real datasets. DCA outperforms existing methods for data imputation in quality and speed, enhancing biological discovery.","authors":[{"name":"Eraslan G."},{"name":"Mircea M."},{"name":"Mueller N.S."},{"name":"Simon L.M."},{"name":"Theis F.J."}],"citationCount":160,"date":"2019-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Communications","title":"Single-cell RNA-seq denoising using a deep count autoencoder"},"pmcid":"PMC6344535","pmid":"30674886","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Statistics and probability","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2269"},{"term":"Transcriptomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3308"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"DCA","home":"https://bio.tools/DCA","license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"Deep count autoencoder for denoising scRNA-seq data.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:dca/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":true,"registration":false},"packages":true,"source_packages":true,"sourcecode":{"free":true,"interpreted":true,"license":true,"public":true,"readme":true,"repository":{"anonymous":true,"online":true}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"training_material":true},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":517,"citations":[{"count":2,"year":"-1"},{"count":4,"year":"2018"},{"count":21,